# Byte-preserving checkout on every platform.
#
# `* -text` disables git's end-of-line conversion for every file in this repository:
# nothing is normalised on commit and nothing is rewritten on checkout, so a working
# tree is byte-for-byte what was deposited.
#
# This matters because the deposit is verified by checksum. README.md tells a reader to
# run `shasum -a 256 -c MANIFEST.sha256` before reproducing the analysis. On Windows,
# git's default `core.autocrlf=true` would rewrite line endings at checkout, changing the
# bytes of every LF file and so its SHA-256 digest. Each rewritten file would then fail
# the manifest check, which reads as a corrupted download rather than as a platform
# artefact. This line prevents that.
#
# Do not replace this with per-extension `text`/`eol` rules: any rule that normalises
# line endings reintroduces the same failure.

* -text
